                            to World Heritage listing.
                        </p> -->
                    </div>

                    <div class="sub-desc-img">
                        <p>
                            In October 2012, the Hoeamsaji Museum opened. With the archaeological excavations results upto 2015, the museum initiated its own in-house research.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            In October 2016, the Comprehensive Maintenance Project for Hoeamsaji was completed in almost 20 yeas. Subsequently, a master plan to push for the World Heritage inscription of Hoeamsaji was established, signaling the official beginning of the nomination process. Close consultations with related organizations and heritage experts followed.
                        </p>

                        <h4>
                            Pushing for World Heritage Inscription
                        </h4>

                        <div class="history-list">

                            <article class="history-item">
                                <div class="history-year">2015</div>
                                <div class="history-content">
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>
                                            <span>-</span>
                                            Consultation with World Heritage experts and in-house museum research conducted
                                        </li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </article>

                            <article class="history-item">
                                <div class="history-year">2016</div>
                                <div class="history-content">
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>
                                            <span>-</span>
                                            Plan set up to promote the inscription of the Yangju Hoeamsaji on the UNESCO World Heritage List
                                        </li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </article>

